**Dq:** The ⁴A₂→⁴T₂ band is ν₁ = 10Dq, so Dq = 17 500 / 10 = **1750 cm⁻¹**. This follows directly from the octahedral d³ model.

**B and C:** I could not determine these reliably. Solving them needs the full d³ Tanabe–Sugano energy matrices, and I could not reconstruct the off-diagonal ⁴T₁ elements with confidence. My trial matrix gave unphysical values (B ≈ 2900 cm⁻¹), so I have not reported numbers for them. The ²E band (14 300 cm⁻¹) would also constrain C, but I could not verify the ²E energy expression, so I have not used it either. Solving the 4T₁(F) and ²E energies simultaneously against the full Tanabe–Sugano matrices, with Dq = 1750 cm⁻¹ fixed, would give B and C.

